+        // namespace with two settings then had two [ns] sections, and GetPrivateProfileInt only
+        // searches the FIRST: the second key always read as absent, so every boot appended
+        // another block and the value the user edited was ignored. That silently defeated the
+        // [EquipExtension] Enabled kill switch (Zeppelin 2026-09-20). The description is written
+        // once, as a comment line above the section, only when the section is new.
         void WriteDefault(const char* ns, const char* key, const char* description, bool defaultValue) noexcept
         {
