From 709f1ea4f6abde652bcb9e44abad40204a26eb1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 06:48:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] fix: F-211 - evict by build round, not by re-reading
 the dispatch buffer

The 2026-09-20 bleed fix re-read the dispatch's item-data pointer every 100 ms and
dropped the attachment when the value changed. The client's own log shows that
pointer is a transient buffer: the SAME address for every slot of one character
build, a different one next build. The re-read therefore never matched and the
purge deleted every attachment it had just made - 21 purges x 4 entries in one
session, which is why boots and gloves (and the rest) showed only painted texture.

That same property makes the pointer a reliable BUILD-ROUND marker. Each entry now
records the buffer it came from, and a dispatch from a different buffer drops the
entries left from the earlier round: stale after a rebuild, and the previous
character's gear once WoW recycles the address. The per-frame re-read is gone.
